skibidi main
{
    🚽 the issue's own migration example: the initializer references the
    🚽 variable it is declaring. n must already exist by the time slorp's
    🚽 argument is evaluated, or the argument silently evaluates to nothing
    🚽 and this reads 0 instead of stdin (the pre-fix bug: the ast_accept
    🚽 pre-visit ran slorp(n) before interpreter_visit_declaration had
    🚽 created n).
    rizz n = slorp(n);
    yapping("n=%d", n);
    bussin 0;
}
